<title>DENMARK: Danish July trade surplus 1.121 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish July trade surplus 1.121 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 1.121 billion crowns in July 1996 compared to a revised 2.913 billion crowns in June 1996, the national statistics office said on Friday.  </p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			     July 1996    June 1996  July 1995</p>
<p> Exports			 20.482	 23.267     18.231</p>
<p> Imports			 18.961	 20.100     16.718</p>
<p> Trade balance		  1.521	  3.167	1.513</p>
<p> Trade balance excl ships   1.121	  2.913	1.451</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	  2.318	  1.503	2.158</p>
<p>balance excluding ships</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters on average forecast a July surplus excluding ships of 1.9 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
